 "sources": {
  "clock_meridiem_night": [
   "The NIGHT daypart is a midnight-crossing BAND in colloquial clock usage,",
   "not a uniform +12 PM shift: \"la una de nueyt\" is 01:00, \"las diez de nueyt\"",
   "is 22:00, twelve is midnight 00:00.  Small hours 1..5 stay AM, evening",
   "hours 6..11 are PM, twelve is midnight (band-split in resolver _clock_hms).",
   "AN is Ibero-Romance and shares the same madrugada band [00:00, 06:00) as",
   "es/ca/pt (chronologia/dayparts.py); the 5|6 cut is inherited from the",
   "RAE/DIEC/Priberam-cited boundary for the sibling Ibero-Romance locales",
   "(see chronologia/locale/es/clock_meridiem_night.voc) pending native",
   "confirmation for Aragonese (tracked in issue #266)."
  ],
  "marker_during": [
   "\"en\" is the locative preposition used with months (\"en chinero\").",
   "Source: Diccionario aragones, https://academiadelaragones.org/."
  ],
  "marker_year_plural": [
   "The plural year noun that frames a decade (\"os anyos 80\"); the singular",
   "\"anyo\" names a single year and must not reach the decade slot.",
   "Source: Wiktionary, s.v. \"anyo\" (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anyo),",
   "Aragonese noun: \"anyo m (plural anyos)\", citing the Aragonario,",
   "diccionario castellano-aragones."
  ],
  "scope_unit_century": [
   "Wiktionary \"sieglo\" (en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sieglo): Aragonese masculine",
   "noun \"century\", plural \"sieglos\", a semi-learned borrowing from Latin",
   "saeculum."
  ],
  "scope_unit_decade": [
   "Wiktionary \"decada\" (en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decada): Aragonese feminine",
   "noun \"decade (10 years)\", synonym of \"decenio\" -- both listed."
  ],
  "unit_century": [
   "Wiktionary \"sieglo\" (en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sieglo): Aragonese masculine",
   "noun \"century\", plural \"sieglos\", a semi-learned borrowing from Latin",
   "saeculum."
  ],
  "unit_decade": [
   "Wiktionary \"decada\" (en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decada): Aragonese feminine",
   "noun \"decade (10 years)\", synonym of \"decenio\" -- both listed."
